BossNPC: {
	DisplayName: Trial Officer
	Name.BossNPC: ""
	PortraitName: Trial Officer

	Chat: {
		Normal1: Hello, Trialist. Anything you need for battle or adventure?
		Normal2: I've been traveling this world for a while, and I've found a few rather interesting trial targets. Would you like to take them on?
		Normal3: Trialist, once you've switched to new weapons and gear, don't forget to try them out on a target dummy.
		Normal4: Taking a break now and then isn't a bad idea, you know. There's an old saying back home: rest is part of the fight.
		Normal5: I'll let you in on the single most important rule: if you meet an enemy you cannot beat — just run. I don't consider that shameful in the slightest. In fact, I'd call it a remarkably sound decision.
		Normal6: Many people fight without ever stopping — for victory, honor, money, status... I've even met someone whose reason was the purest of all: "Can I win, just this once?" And honestly, I'm curious too, my dear Trialist — what are you fighting for?
		Normal7: What, you're asking why someone called a Trial Officer looks like this? Because... I have another profession as well. As for what it is — that's a secret. All I can tell you is that it has something to do with the [c/FF467B:God]. Anything beyond that, you'll have to guess.
		NoBoss: I've been traveling this world for a while, and I've found a few rather interesting trial targets. Would you like to take them on?
		KingSlime00: A soft lump of gel like that, and he still gets to call himself a king? Honestly, that's a little absurd. Still, his bouncing does make good practice for reading where a target will land.
		EyeOfCthulhu00: I didn't expect a monster like the Eye of Cthulhu to exist in this world as well. Still, the pause before it dives is actually good practice for your footwork, since you have to read the dive before it starts. Anyway, well done, Trialist.
		BrainOfCthulhu00: Illusions and teleporting tricks from a giant brain. On a battlefield, that's called psychological warfare. You didn't lose your footing, and you saw straight through the trick. Your focus and your intuition deserve credit.
		EaterOfWorlds00: That worm reeking of evil — the Eater of Worlds. In my view, a body that big usually comes with a weakness just as big. And I could see you made full use of it in the end.
		QueenBee00: In [c/C5EEFF:Bee World], that place where giant bees are everywhere, the Queen Bee's sting and her charges stopped being anything new long ago. In my view, what really bears down on your mind is the deafening drone that blankets the whole sky when she beats those enormous insect wings.
		Skeletron00: It looks like that skull in the dungeon is guarding the dignity of a dungeon door. What sustains him and holds him bound, obsession or a curse?
		Deerclops00: That beast called the Deerclops gives me a sense of something that doesn't belong to this world. But fighting it really tests how much punishment you can take, and the nerve to face something that size head-on.
		WallOfFlesh00: A crack has opened in the wall of the world. To a true Trialist, that isn't an ending, the battlefield has simply been expanded. The opponents ahead will be much harder to deal with. Still, judging by the potential you've shown so far, I'd much rather see them turn out to be nothing more than a fresh batch of tougher punching bags to you.
		QueenSlime00: If I'm to judge, Queen Slime's own fighting strength isn't in the top bracket. But send her in with a whole swarm of little minions, and she's a real pain! Still, you handled it cleanly in the end, so here's a thumbs up for you.
		TheDestroyer00: The Destroyer is like one long steel earthworm. Beating it means your piercing power has passed the bar. But tell me, have you ever heard the sound of a projectile running straight through its whole body? That crisp shatter of metal and gears, if you find it pleasing to the ear, then that means... it means you were born a hunter~
		TheTwins00: The Twins, two horrifying eyeballs, two rhythms pushed to their extremes. I'm glad to see you can take on both at once, which means you've become a truly outstanding Trialist!
		SkeletronPrime00: Skeletron Prime is like a revenant pieced together from steel and gears. Honestly, its spinning is even more dizzying than the one in the dungeon.
		Plantera00: That giant bulb is the oldest being in the jungle. Perhaps she carries world history within her, worth tracing back and examining? Good thing she's awake now. We have plenty of time to "ask her"!
		EmpressOfLight00: The queen of the Hallowed — the Empress of Light. The light she scatters is as dense as a driving storm. To keep pace and strike back under that kind of speed and that barrage of projectiles, your dynamic vision and your split-second reflexes are already those of a first-rate fighter... Honestly, I'm astonished.
		Golem00: In my view, with a body that huge, every punch the Golem brings down would feel to an ordinary person like the ground splitting apart. To find the weakness under that kind of absolute pressure and keep your footing, your nerve and your composure already outstrip most of the Trialists whose names are known.
		DukeFishron00: Duke Fishron, a big fish gone mad in the middle of a storm. It gives me that same feeling as standing face to face with the predators of the [c/C5EEFF:Dream Sea]. Still, surviving its wild charges tells me your footwork and your dodging are already beyond reproach.
		Cultist00: To have come this far, I'd say you already stand out as one of the finest among Trialists. They say that behind the Lunatic Cultist there is more than a mob of fanatics who have lost all control, that something far beyond comprehension and reason stands behind them. And now I have a feeling that your trial is about to reach a major turning point.
		MoonLord00: I'm so astonished. Your skill in battle and your strength have climbed to such a height that even that horrifying thing from the moon has fallen to you. Could it be that you are the [c/FF467B:Player] of legend? Don't misunderstand. The ordinary people of every world and every nation mostly don't know this particular title at all. Only the very few who are close to the [c/FF467B:God] ever learn it. In any case, there is one thing I can be sure of: The [c/FF467B:Player] holds a strength far beyond everyone else's, and limitless potential. As for what the word "player" actually means... honestly, I don't know either.
		KingSlime0: A soft lump of gel like that, and he still gets to call himself a king? Honestly, that's a little absurd. Still, his bouncing does make good practice for reading where a target will land.
		KingSlime1: The King Slime has a habit of constantly pulling itself back together. Some biologists would love to research that, but I've always held that he never really died. Otherwise, just look. This world is still full of slimes hopping about.
		EyeOfCthulhu0: I didn't expect a monster like the Eye of Cthulhu to exist in this world as well. Still, the pause before it dives is actually good practice for your footwork, since you have to read the dive before it starts. Anyway, well done, Trialist.
		EyeOfCthulhu1: That big eyeball... I've seen monsters like it in other worlds too. In some of them people call it "the rookie examiner". Where do you stand on that? ...Hmm? What do you mean, lying down?
		BrainOfCthulhu0: Illusions and teleporting tricks from a giant brain. On a battlefield, that's called psychological warfare. You didn't lose your footing, and you saw straight through the trick. Your focus and your intuition deserve credit.
		EaterOfWorlds0: That worm reeking of evil — the Eater of Worlds. In my view, a body that big usually comes with a weakness just as big. And I could see you made full use of it in the end.
		QueenBee0: In [c/C5EEFF:Bee World], that place where giant bees are everywhere, the Queen Bee's sting and her charges stopped being anything new long ago. In my view, what really bears down on your mind is the deafening drone that blankets the whole sky when she beats those enormous insect wings.
		Skeletron0: It looks like that skull in the dungeon is guarding the dignity of a dungeon door. What sustains him and holds him bound, obsession or a curse?
		Deerclops0: That beast called the Deerclops gives me a sense of something that doesn't belong to this world. But fighting it really tests how much punishment you can take, and the nerve to face something that size head-on.
		WallOfFlesh0: A crack has opened in the wall of the world. To a true Trialist, that isn't an ending, the battlefield has simply been expanded. The opponents ahead will be much harder to deal with. Still, judging by the potential you've shown so far, I'd much rather see them turn out to be nothing more than a fresh batch of tougher punching bags to you.
		QueenSlime0: If I'm to judge, Queen Slime's own fighting strength isn't in the top bracket. But send her in with a whole swarm of little minions, and she's a real pain! Still, you handled it cleanly in the end, so here's a thumbs up for you.
		TheDestroyer0: The Destroyer is like one long steel earthworm. Beating it means your piercing power has passed the bar. But tell me, have you ever heard the sound of a projectile running straight through its whole body? That crisp shatter of metal and gears, if you find it pleasing to the ear, then that means... it means you were born a hunter~
		TheTwins0: The Twins, two horrifying eyeballs, two rhythms pushed to their extremes. I'm glad to see you can take on both at once, which means you've become a truly outstanding Trialist!
		SkeletronPrime0: Skeletron Prime is like a revenant pieced together from steel and gears. Honestly, its spinning is even more dizzying than the one in the dungeon.
		Plantera0: That giant bulb is the oldest being in the jungle. Perhaps she carries world history within her, worth tracing back and examining? Good thing she's awake now. We have plenty of time to "ask her"!
		EmpressOfLight0: The queen of the Hallowed — the Empress of Light. The light she scatters is as dense as a driving storm. To keep pace and strike back under that kind of speed and that barrage of projectiles, your dynamic vision and your split-second reflexes are already those of a first-rate fighter... Honestly, I'm astonished.
		Golem0: In my view, with a body that huge, every punch the Golem brings down would feel to an ordinary person like the ground splitting apart. To find the weakness under that kind of absolute pressure and keep your footing, your nerve and your composure already outstrip most of the Trialists whose names are known.
		DukeFishron0: Duke Fishron, a big fish gone mad in the middle of a storm. It gives me that same feeling as standing face to face with the predators of the [c/C5EEFF:Dream Sea]. Still, surviving its wild charges tells me your footwork and your dodging are already beyond reproach.
		Cultist0: To have come this far, I'd say you already stand out as one of the finest among Trialists. They say that behind the Lunatic Cultist there is more than a mob of fanatics who have lost all control, that something far beyond comprehension and reason stands behind them. And now I have a feeling that your trial is about to reach a major turning point.
		MoonLord0: I'm so astonished. Your skill in battle and your strength have climbed to such a height that even that horrifying thing from the moon has fallen to you. Could it be that you are the [c/FF467B:Player] of legend? Don't misunderstand. The ordinary people of every world and every nation mostly don't know this particular title at all. Only the very few who are close to the [c/FF467B:God] ever learn it. In any case, there is one thing I can be sure of: The [c/FF467B:Player] holds a strength far beyond everyone else's, and limitless potential. As for what the word "player" actually means... honestly, I don't know either.
		MoonLord1: You're asking whether that big squid from the moon counts as a [c/FF467B:God]? Going by the state He was in while alive, and by the mark His death left on the world, I'd say at best He was a false god...
	}

