PotionNPC: {
	DisplayName: Elixir Brewer
	Name.PotionNPC: Little Ghostie
	PortraitName: Elixir Brewer Little Ghostie

	Chat: {
		Normal1: Hello. I can feel it, your soul isn't quite like other people's. I was taught from a young age that people like that are worth respecting. If you have a moment, please have a look and see if there's anything in my shop you'd like!
		Normal2_Male: Mister, I just brewed a new potion, but I'm not sure how well it works... Would you like to try it? No, no, please don't worry! It won't have any horrible side effects or anything, I promise. I only used ordinary herbs, the kind you can find anywhere, picked right here in this world.
		Normal2_Female: Miss, I just brewed a new potion, but I'm not sure how well it works... Would you like to try it? No, no, please don't worry! It won't have any horrible side effects or anything, I promise. I only used ordinary herbs, the kind you can find anywhere, picked right here in this world.
		Normal3_Male: Mister, if you're going off somewhere far away, could you... tell me in advance? I only want to have plenty of potions ready, for when you come back safe.
		Normal3_Female: Miss, if you're going off somewhere far away, could you... tell me in advance? I only want to have plenty of potions ready, for when you come back safe.
		Normal4: Morning dew is the best thing for watering Dayblooms. But I always get up too early, and the dew on the leaves soaks through my cloak. If you need a potion that keeps the sleepiness away during the day, please come and find me.
		Normal5: The gel that slimes drop, and the materials you get from some monsters... you might not believe it, but even though they look a little frightening, they all make very good medicine. Please, whatever you do, don't throw them away.
		Normal6: You're asking why I dress like this? Back home, the night takes up almost the whole day, and it's cold and damp, and we live right by the river. So going out in a thick short cloak keeps the chill off, and it's easier to move around in, too.
		Normal7: The people of my homeland have passed down the craft of "birthing souls" for generation after generation. And because of that, my home was coveted, and then invaded. There was a terrible war. I was lucky. People shielded me, and I ran, all the way to your world.
		Normal8: Whenever I think back on my homeland, the first thing that comes to mind is the Soulcradle River, long and winding, and somehow comforting. They say at the very end of that river, at the Soulcradle Source, there's a giant waterfall that stretches across the sky. It's meant to be magnificent. If I get the chance, I'd like to take you to see it!
		Night0: If you're going out at night, please... be careful of those flying eyeballs. They aren't deadly, but they look so frightening. I did try going out at night once, to pick Moonglow, but the moment I saw a pair of red wings flying toward me, I ran straight back inside... please, please don't laugh at me.
		Night1: The fireflies at night are beautiful, like flying stars. Back home, I used to lean over the windowsill and just watch them, spacing out... I love lights like that in the dark. They make me think of warm things, and hopeful things.
		HardMode0: I can feel it, faintly, the light inside you is brighter than when we first met. Back home the elders called that the growth of a soul. You must have been through so many battles...
	}

