BuildNPC: {
	DisplayName: Architect Scholar
	Name.BuildNPC: QiaoQiao
	PortraitName: Architect Scholar QiaoQiao

	Chat: {
		Normal1: Dirt blocks might not be worth anything to you, since it's everywhere around here. But in some worlds, a world of nothing but minerals, for instance, that little patch of dirt is worth a king's ransom! After all... things are precious exactly because they're rare.
		Normal2: Why do I carry a hammer around? Because a hammer can smash old walls and seat new bricks. Much more dependable than a wrench! Of course, I do set it down when I sleep...
		Normal3: If you're planning to build a house, you have to remember one iron rule: a solid foundation matters more than the roof, and a roof that keeps out wind and rain matters more than the walls. But then — sturdy walls absolutely matter more than the foundation! Um... so really, not one of them can be left out~
		Normal4: If you ever want to build something truly grand, remember to call me in. I'll bring my hammer and my measuring tape, and with the most precise calculations and a strict "knock test", I guarantee your house will come out sturdier than a king's castle!
		Normal5: My homeland, um... the truth is, the reason I left was that I felt the country I was born in was, well, "not quite right". The way its society and technology were heading was a little unsettling. And I never liked those gears that rust and break down anyway. Cement and stone bricks just feel safer...
		Normal6: So, tell me... a whole city built out of clockwork and machinery and gears... why would it ever go in that direction? I still haven't worked it out. Could it be that I always dozed off in history class, and missed some crucial turning point?
	}

